  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Autonomous Disaster Information Collection System",
    "description": "Firefighting is a dangerous and deadly occupation that has to be done to keep the general public safe.  The largest danger to firefighters is a lack of situational information about the nature of the fire and the building.  The proposal is for an autonomous situational data scout that has the ability to find the exact location of the fire in the building, any occupants and do this all before the arrival of the fire department.  Upon arrival the firefighters would be given this information in the form of a real time display aiding in the elimination of the fire and the rescue of any occupants.  The system will be a distributed redundant fault tolerant network of flying robots.  These robots will contains sensors from temperature to CO2 giving the widest range of information, they will also be equip with cameras feeding a live video stream to the firefighting team.  With a system such as proposed, lives can be saved, and the dangerous job of firefighting can be made safer.",
